{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"dff08a33a217b0e424b2c16c4831a38183890efa4c552790a4d65d2d47aef1b9","packTokens":2792,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":240,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":698,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1533,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using their Folio3 Google account, with employee profiles and vehicle details populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking with a single action and view its status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can schedule or cancel parking releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can view availability and claim released parking on a first-come, first-served basis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and generate and email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"When an employee with multiple registered vehicles claims temporary parking, which vehicle's plate should be authorized for that day's allocation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The employee selects one registered vehicle when claiming; only that plate is authorized for the allocation.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which timezone defines “today,” the 30-day scheduling window, the daily release time, and Monday-morning report scheduling?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the office's local timezone for all date boundaries and scheduled times.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the system choose the assigned parking floor when it automatically allocates a claimed space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Choose a floor with the most remaining capacity, using a consistent tie-break when floors are equally available.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Which sources should provide the employee, vehicle, and parking-assignment records, and how should existing records be loaded?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the corporate directory for employee identity and an administrator-maintained parking/vehicle roster for assignments, initially loaded from existing records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How long should release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history be retained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply Folio3's existing records-retention policy to these histories.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"If a dedicated holder arrives in a vehicle with a permanent parking sticker after releasing their space and another employee has claimed it, which access outcome should apply?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Honor the permanent sticker holder's entry; the temporary claimant may be denied if the released space is occupied.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Which dates count as working days for the default dedicated-parking availability and related utilization scenarios?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat Monday through Friday as working days, without excluding holidays.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"What parking information should security guards be able to access beyond the indicator result at the entrance?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only use the indicator; do not provide guards with a product screen or parking records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall authenticate employees only through Folio3 Google Workspace accounts, reject personal Gmail and other non-Folio3 identities, and show returning employees their dashboard.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"On sign-in, the app shall retrieve employee profiles by corporate email from the corporate directory and populate employee details, parking assignments, and registered vehicle details from the administrator-maintained roster, including an initial load of existing records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"For employees without dedicated parking and without a registered vehicle, the app shall require at least one license plate before allowing claims, support one or more plates with optional make, model, and color, and activate each new plate immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall treat Monday through Friday as working days, including holidays, and Saturday and Sunday as non-working days when applying default dedicated-parking availability and utilization scenarios.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"A dedicated parking holder shall be able to release today's assigned space in one action; the app shall reject duplicate releases and releases by ineligible employees or for claimed spaces, and expose space status as Reserved, Released, or Claimed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders shall be able to schedule one or more releases up to 30 calendar days ahead, view saved releases on a calendar, and cancel a scheduled release only while its space is unclaimed; the app shall record scheduling and cancellation events.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall default the daily parking release time to 8:00 AM in the office's local timezone and allow an administrator to configure that time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall evaluate today, the 30-day scheduling window, daily release cutoffs, and weekly report scheduling using the configured office-local timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Scheduled releases and same-day releases made before the daily release time shall make spaces claimable at that time; same-day releases made after that time shall make spaces available immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall show available-space counts and allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee whose claim is accepted, allowing each space to be claimed only once; employees with dedicated parking cannot claim temporary spaces.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Employees claiming temporary parking shall select one registered vehicle; only that vehicle's plate shall be authorized for the allocation, and the app shall assign a floor with the most remaining capacity using a consistent tie-break.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When parking spaces become available, the app shall email eligible employees without dedicated parking using a fixed-template message.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"In Phase 1, the app shall reject employee cancellation of an active temporary parking claim.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"When the existing entrance LPR camera reports a car plate detection, the app shall verify authorization for the office-local date, activate the green indicator only for valid temporary authorization, and record each verification attempt with date, time, plate, result, and entry status; detections of non-car objects shall receive no parking authorization result and trigger no green activation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall record permanent-sticker vehicle plate detections for utilization, bypass temporary authorization and entry blocking for those detections, and limit guard-facing access to the indicator result without exposing parking records or other product screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"If the camera, plate recognition, network, or indicator fails, or a plate cannot be read, the app shall issue no automatic green authorization and record an unsuccessful verification result for manual handling.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"For each working day when a dedicated holder did not release the space and no registered vehicle entry was detected, the app shall record an Unused Dedicated Parking event; it shall record an Unused Temporary Parking event when a claimant's selected vehicle was not detected entering on the claim date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall generate a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office timezone, containing the specified dedicated- and temporary-unused employee lists, daily and weekly statistics, total released spaces, total temporary claims, and overall utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall email each weekly report to the designated stakeholders and permit only authenticated parking administrators to update the stakeholder recipient list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"In Phase 1, utilization shall not trigger automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall retain release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history according to Folio3's existing records-retention policy.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"The product shall be one responsive web app with layouts for phone, tablet, and desktop; pages shall avoid horizontal overflow at representative widths and narrow layouts shall use touch-sized controls.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}